# addPagination

`addPagination` paginates the table by page index.

<Admonition type="note">Render <a href="/docs/api/table-view-model#tableviewmodel-current-pagerows-bodyrow"><code>vm.current.pageRows</code></a> instead of <code>vm.current.rows</code>.</Admonition>

```svelte {5,11}
<script>
  const vm = table.createViewModel(columns)
</script>

<table>
  <tbody>
    {#each vm.current.pageRows as row (row.id)}
      ...
    {/each}
  </tbody>
</table>
```

## Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into <code>addPagination</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const table = createTable(data, {
  page: addPagination({ ... }),
});
```

### `initialPageIndex?: number`
Default `0`.

### `initialPageSize?: number`
Default `10`.

### `serverSide?: boolean`
If `true`, use server-side pagination by updating the table's <a href="/docs/api/create-table#createtable-data-plugins-table">data</a>.

### `serverItemCount: number | (() => number)`
Total item count when using server-side pagination. Required if `serverSide = true`. Pass a getter to make it reactive:

```ts
let total = $state(0)
const table = createTable(() => items, {
  page: addPagination({ serverSide: true, serverItemCount: () => total }),
})
```

A Svelte store is rejected with an error. If the count lives in a store you do not own, wrap it with `fromStore` in your own code and pass `() => wrapped.current`.

## Column Options

<Admonition type="info">Options passed into column definitions.</Admonition>

```ts {7}
const columns = table.createColumns([
  table.column({
    header: 'Name',
    accessor: 'name',
    plugins: {
      page: { ... },
    },
  }),
]);
```

## Prop Set

<Admonition type="info">Extensions to the view model. Read <code>current.props</code> on table components.</Admonition>

```svelte
{#each vm.current.headerRows as headerRow (headerRow.id)}
  {headerRow.current.props.page}
  {#each headerRow.cells as cell (cell.id)}
    {cell.current.props.page}
  {/each}
{/each}
```

## Interactions

- Page size counts every row `pageRows` receives: group header rows from `addGroupBy` and expanded children from `addExpandedRows` both take a slot.
- Sorting and filtering run before pagination, so `pageCount` reflects the filtered, sorted set.

## Plugin State

<Admonition type="info">State provided by <code>addPagination</code>.</Admonition>

```ts {3}
const vm = table.createViewModel(columns)
const { pluginStates } = vm
const { pageIndex, pageSize, pageCount, hasPreviousPage, hasNextPage } = pluginStates.page
```

### `pageSize: Box<number>`
The page size. Writes below `1` are clamped to `1`.

### `pageIndex: Box<number>`
The page index, 0-based. The value you write is kept, but reads are clamped to the last page, so shrinking the data or growing the page size never shows an empty page.

### `pageCount: ReadonlyBox<number>`
The total number of pages.

### `hasPreviousPage: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`
### `hasNextPage: ReadonlyBox<boolean>`

```svelte
<button onclick={() => (pageIndex.current -= 1)} disabled={!hasPreviousPage.current}>
  Previous page
</button>
{pageIndex.current + 1} out of {pageCount.current}
<button onclick={() => (pageIndex.current += 1)} disabled={!hasNextPage.current}>
  Next page
</button>
<input type="number" min={1} bind:value={pageSize.current} />
```

`createPageState({ items, initialPageSize, initialPageIndex, serverSide, serverItemCount })`, where `items` is a getter for the rows to paginate, builds the same state outside a table. It replaces the 6.x `createPageStore`.

